2. Understand embeddings
Imagine you have these three sentences:
1.	"I want to learn artificial intelligence."
2.	"I am interested in machine learning."
3.	"The weather is very hot today."
A traditional keyword search might fail to recognize that sentences 1 and 2 are related because they don't share many exact words.
An embedding model converts each sentence into a numerical vector representing its semantic meaning.
Example (illustrative numbers only):
