12. Interview preparation
These are important questions for an AI Platform Engineer interview.
Q1. What are embeddings?
Embeddings are numerical representations of data, such as text, images or audio. They capture semantic characteristics and allow similarity-based retrieval.
Q2. What is the difference between keyword search and semantic search?
Keyword search looks for matching words. Semantic search uses vector representations to retrieve content based on meaning.
Q3. What is cosine similarity?
It measures the cosine of the angle between two vectors to estimate their directional similarity.
Q4. What is a vector database?
A database designed to store, index and retrieve vector embeddings efficiently. Examples include ChromaDB, FAISS, Pinecone, Weaviate and Milvus.
Q5. What is the difference between FAISS and ChromaDB?
•	FAISS is a library for efficient similarity search over dense vectors.
•	ChromaDB provides vector storage, metadata, document management and similarity-query capabilities.
Q6. Why do we store metadata with embeddings?
Metadata helps filter and organize search results by user, document, category, source or other attributes.
Q7. What happens when a user submits a search query?
The application generates an embedding for the query, searches for similar stored vectors, retrieves matching documents and returns their associated text and metadata.
